outputs.L1:
A system and method are provided for reliably monitoring a parameter, in particular a moment of inertia, required for determining the kinetic energy of an object measurable by means of a sensor of a coordinate measuring machine. The object is moved between various positions, preferably being at least briefly at rest at each approach position. The method comprises the steps of:

a) initially determining the parameter and setting the initially determined parameter as a target value;

b) moving the object from one position to a next position and re-determining the parameter for a movement cycle between the corresponding positions;

c) setting the re-determined parameter as an actual value;

d) comparing the target value with the actual value;

e) continuing movement of the object if the comparison indicates that the actual value substantially coincides with the target value, and returning to step b) as long as a last position has not been reached; or

f) outputting an error message if the comparison indicates that the actual value deviates significantly from the target value.

counterfactuals.output:
A system and method are provided for reliably monitoring a parameter required to determine the kinetic energy of a moving object. The system includes at least one sensor configured to detect an actual value of the parameter, a controller configured to compare the actual value with a target value or permissible target range, and an output or safety device configured to generate a signal or initiate an action when the comparison indicates an unacceptable deviation.

In one embodiment, the method includes:

a) detecting, by at least one sensor, an actual value of a parameter associated with a moving object, the parameter being usable to determine kinetic energy of the object;

b) providing a target value or target value range for the parameter;

c) comparing the detected actual value with the target value or target value range;

d) determining whether the actual value deviates from the target value or target value range by more than a predefined tolerance;

e) generating a monitoring, warning, correction, or shutdown signal when the deviation exceeds the predefined tolerance; and

f) storing, transmitting, or using the comparison result to determine or validate kinetic energy of the moving object.

By continuously or periodically comparing the actual value with the target value, the system enables reliable monitoring of the parameter and improves the accuracy and safety of kinetic-energy determination.
